<div class="wrap narrow prose" lang="en">
  <p><span class="badge badge--accent">Monday 23 November 2026</span> <span class="badge">Brussels</span></p>
  {% include "partials/countdown.njk" %}

  <h2 id="what">What and where?</h2>
  <p>A <strong>national demonstration by the joint union front</strong> against austerity which, in the unions' words, once again puts the burden “on workers, benefit recipients and public services”. Time and starting point will be announced by the unions: check the official channels of the <a href="https://www.lacsc.be/" rel="noopener">CSC</a>, <a href="https://fgtb.be/" rel="noopener">FGTB</a> and <a href="https://www.synova.be/" rel="noopener">Synova</a>, or ask your union rep. {% src "rtbf-23nov" %}</p>
  <p><a class="btn btn--accent" href="/agenda/manif-nationale-23-novembre.ics" download>{% icon "calendar" %} Add to your calendar (.ics)</a></p>

  <h2 id="why">Why?</h2>
  <ul class="facts">
    <li><strong>Your wages:</strong> in 2026 and 2028, automatic wage indexation is capped for gross salaries above €4,000 a month (and for benefits and pensions above €2,000). On 15 October, Prime Minister De Wever even proposed freezing all indexation for a year (not adopted). Inflation hit 5.26% in October 2026. {% src "rtbf-accord-2025" %} {% src "rtbf-gel-index" %} {% src "te-inflation-oct" %}</li>
    <li><strong>Your pension:</strong> from 2027, a penalty of up to 25% for early retirement without 35 years of at least 156 working days. Part-time workers, mostly women, are hit hardest. {% src "csc-temps-partiel" %}</li>
    <li><strong>Unemployment:</strong> benefits are now limited in time; 168,063 people had reached the end of their entitlement by February 2026. {% src "lalibre-exclus" %}</li>
    <li><strong>Schools, healthcare and public services</strong> are under pressure — and so is the right to protest.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="money">The money exists</h2>
  <p>The unions have costed <strong>€21.2 billion</strong> of alternatives, including €12.9 billion (Federal Planning Bureau estimate) by taxing all income the same way. The richest 10% of households own 54.9% of net wealth. {% src "lalibre-alternatives" %} {% src "forum-patrimoine" %}</p>

  <h2 id="now">Why now?</h2>
  <p>On 2 November, the coalition failed to agree on the budget — precisely over who should contribute more: “the broadest shoulders” or not. The Prime Minister offered his resignation; the King put his decision on hold. The 2027 budget will be decided in the coming weeks. {% src "vrt-crise" %}</p>

  <h2 id="history">Every right was fought for</h2>
  <p>Universal suffrage (general strike of 1893), the eight-hour day (1921), paid holidays (1936 strike), social security (1944): nothing was given. <a href="/histoire/">See the timeline (FR)</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="rights">Your rights</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The right to strike applies to everyone, union member or not (European Social Charter, art. 6 §4). Union members receive strike pay. {% src "degand-greve" %}</li>
    <li>Administrative arrest: 12 hours maximum. Judicial arrest: 48 hours maximum. {% src "droitsquotidiens-arrest" %}</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="join">Join in</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Save the date: 23 November.</li>
    <li>Talk to three colleagues or neighbours.</li>
    <li>Ask your union rep about group departures.</li>
    <li>Come to Brussels, and bring someone along.</li>
  </ol>
